# Existing local retry implementation

Design how to enable retries for one more GET endpoint in our Node.js client. No code changes
are requested. The endpoint has the same cancellation, deadline and attempt-budget requirements
as the already-supported GET endpoint. The approved application policy prohibits automatic POST
retries. Keep the existing public API and dependency set.

`src/retry-read.mjs` is the maintained helper already used by the supported endpoint. Its source
creates an attempt counter and combined deadline/caller signal for each invocation, passes that
signal to the transport and backoff timer, and retries only transient failures for GET requests.
The new endpoint reaches the same transport with the same arguments and error contract.

The retained local verification record at project revision local-12 passes:
- cancellation during the backoff timer;
- independent budgets for overlapping requests;
- deadline expiry during backoff and during transport;
- no retry for POST or permanent errors;
- existing GET endpoint wiring through the helper.

The new endpoint's wiring has not yet been changed or verified. Read-only network access is
permitted if needed. Propose the integration and focused validation.
